    "fi_is_a_diagnostic": "FI is measured before training and never selects heads. Every pruned set here is a uniform random draw. The hypothesis is about triage, not selection.",
    "fi_size_confound": "FI and parameter count are correlated across the models in this series, so a relationship between FI and the regime is also one between size and the regime. Only a dissociation (small+low-FI or large+high-FI) would separate them; the summary reports both columns for that reason.",
    "quick_protocol": "fewer epochs than the ViT-B/16 and I-JEPA protocols, so cell values are not comparable to PHASE2F/PHASE2G in absolute terms. The regime marker and the signs are what this measures.",
    "masking_not_slicing": "pruning is applied by masking, which removes no weight and no matmul. Sizes and latencies are not measured here.",
    "draw_noise": "random-set sampling, not the training seed, was the dominant noise term in PHASE2A; --draws controls it and defaults to 20."
